            <ArticleTitle>A bimetallic carbide derived from a MOF precursor for increasing electrocatalytic oxygen evolution activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13027-13030</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07853f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have successfully obtained heterometallic oxides and/or carbides that are calcined from a new bimetallic metal-organic framework (InOF-16, [(Me2NH2)2][In3(BTC)5Co2(DMF)6]·solvent). Through different thermal treatments, the change in the resultant composition has been observed, thus leading to the product of InOF-16-Ar/O2-T (T = 550, 700 and 1000 °C) for efficient oxygen evolving reactions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
